calls are avoided in the hot path because the allocator can involve
locking, fragmentation, and unpredictable timing. Common alternative:
pre-allocate a fixed-size memory pool at startup and hand out/reclaim
fixed-size blocks from it during runtime, avoiding calls into the
general-purpose allocator during time-critical operations.

